  "contract": "Both frozen Hegel learners use the same separately frozen public object-schema laboratory. Each apparatus starts with empty knowledge and carries its own complete JSON library between eight tasks. Stages0-3 establish symmetric/always total, event, sum and window. Stage4 jointly changes direction to right and activates source_greater, testing composition of a relation type and a quantity predicate. Stage5 changes only measured field names. Stage6 changes only the quantity predicate to source_less while retaining right direction and renamed fields. Stage7 returns to symmetric/always and original field names. The condition and direction are private environment settings, never learner candidate labels or public spec fields. Both complete learning sequences for a seed must stop before either independent terminal evaluation. All failures and their costs remain, with no changes to algorithms, budgets or seeds after formal outcomes. No Code calls belong to this study.",
  "laboratory_contract": "For each existing directed edge, source_greater permits transfer only when measured physical q_source > q_target, source_less uses q_source < q_target, and always adds no quantity gate. Each active edge subtracts k*q_source from its source and adds it to its target, conserving total quantity. These quantities include the existing actuator mapping. Direction, condition and response law stay absent from public specs. Each apparatus keeps its object membership, radius, coupling, actuator curvature, instrument rates and control bounds through all stages; only the declared direction/condition/name changes occur. Three/four objects are balanced six each.",
  "development_evidence": {
    "formal_inclusion": false,
